 responsible for assigning accounts only to authorised staff. Users must protect credentials and may not resell, redistribute, reverse engineer, share access outside the subscribed office, or bypass account and device controls."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"OCR and count review"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Results depend on document structure, scan quality, installed Microsoft Office components, and device performance. OCR output can contain errors. Customers are responsible for reviewing files marked for attention and verifying results before using them for billing, legal, or contractual decisions."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Availability and updates"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The current release requires Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit), a supported Microsoft Word desktop installation for Word-document counting and supported OCR workflows, and sufficient local storage and memory. Internet access is required for initial sign-in, periodic account validation, support, billing, and updates. After a successful validation, eligible active accounts may work offline for up to 24 hours. Document processing runs locally on the customer's computer. Features, supported formats, and technical requirements may change to improve reliability or security."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Subscriptions and cancellation"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The selected plan, included users, monthly or annual billing interval, price, and applicable taxes are presented before payment. Stripe processes payment information and recurring charges. Subscriptions renew automatically at the selected monthly or annual interval on the date shown at checkout and on invoices until cancelled. Customers can cancel renewal through the secure billing portal or by contacting support. Cancellation stops future renewal and access normally continues until the end of the current paid period. Switching between monthly and annual billing is applied at the end of the current billing period unless RoutineOff expressly confirms another arrangement. No pro-rated refund is created solely because a customer cancels before that date, except where required by law or stated in the Cancellation & Refund Policy."}]]}],"$L8","$L9","$La","$Lb","$Lc"]}],"$Ld"]}]]
8:["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Digital delivery"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"After Stripe confirms a successful payment, the system provisions the office and included tool users. The responsible person receives the usernames, temporary passwords, download link, and subscription period at the business email supplied at checkout. Delivery normally occurs within five minutes. If the email has not arrived within 30 minutes, the customer should check the spam folder and contact support without paying again."}]]}]
9:["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Failed payments and service access"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If a renewal payment fails, RoutineOff may provide a short grace period while Stripe retries payment or the customer updates the payment method. Tool access may be paused when the grace period ends. Restoring payment normally reactivates the existing authorised users. RoutineOff may immediately restrict an account for security abuse, unauthorised sharing, fraud, or unlawful use."}]]}]
a:["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Acceptable use"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Users must have the right to process every document they select and must not use the software for unlawful content, unauthorised access, infringement, or attempts to disrupt the service."}]]}]
b:["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Liability"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"To the extent permitted by applicable law, RoutineOff does not guarantee that every file or OCR page will produce a perfect result or that the software will be uninterrupted on every device. Customers remain responsible for reviewing flagged or uncertain outputs and for verifying counts before using them for quotations, billing, legal, or contractual decisions. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded."}]]}]
